---
/**
 * Final CTA — the homepage closes on the free trial, the way it
 * opened: try the product, compare plans, and a quiet email line
 * for anyone who wants a person first.
 */
import { site } from '../config';
import '../styles/home.css';
---

<section class="fcta" id="get-started" aria-labelledby="fcta-title">
  <div class="fcta-inner">
    <p class="h-kicker">Get started</p>
    <h2 class="fcta-title" id="fcta-title">
      Every organization has an economic impact. <span class="brand-em">Make yours visible.</span>
    </h2>
    <!-- This used to open by listing the audience a third time. The hero
         names it, the "Built to adapt" card names it, and this named it
         again 400 words later, which is once every 200 words on a page of
         588. The heading above already carries the idea without the list.
         What a closing block owes a reader is the next step and the cost
         of taking it, so that is all this says now; both halves of the
         second sentence are the terms already published on /pricing. -->
    <p class="fcta-lede">
      Create a free Seed account, bring your documents and see what the model finds. No credit card,
      no expiration, no obligation.
    </p>
    <div class="hero2-cta">
      <a class="btn2 btn2--primary" href="/signup?tier=free">
        Try Lumecon for free <span class="btn2-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
      </a>
      <a class="btn2 btn2--card" href="/pricing">
        Compare plans <span class="btn2-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
      </a>
    </div>
    <p class="fcta-contact">
      Prefer to talk to a person first? <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
